  "notes": "{混雑|こんざつ} describes a state of being overcrowded with people or vehicles. Used for places, roads, and transportation.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- No standard transitive pair\n- Pattern: {混雑|こんざつ}する\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {混雑|こんざつ}している: is congested/crowded\n- {混雑|こんざつ}を{避|さ}ける: to avoid crowds\n- {混雑|こんざつ}{時|じ}: peak hours, rush time\n- {混雑|こんざつ}{緩和|かんわ}: congestion relief\n- {混雑|こんざつ}{状況|じょうきょう}: crowding conditions\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {渋滞|じゅうたい}: traffic jam (specifically for vehicles on roads)\n- {込|こ}み{合|あ}う: to be crowded (verb, often for trains and shops)\n- {満員|まんいん}: full to capacity (trains, theaters)\n\nNOTE:\n{混雑|こんざつ} is used broadly for any kind of crowding. {渋滞|じゅうたい} is specifically for traffic jams on roads.",
